WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.600
Related rates connect quantities that change together in time

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:09.267
As a circular ripple expands, both radius and area change

00:00:09.267 --> 00:00:16.733
Start with the geometric relationship between them before inserting the numerical information for one particular instant.

00:00:18.033 --> 00:00:20.927
Differentiate the area equation with respect to time

00:00:20.927 --> 00:00:24.182
The chain rule contributes the radius's rate of change

00:00:24.182 --> 00:00:32.500
When the radius is two and grows at half a unit per second, the area grows at two pi square units per second.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:40.655
For a sliding ladder of length five, horizontal and vertical distances satisfy the Pythagorean theorem

00:00:40.655 --> 00:00:44.311
Differentiate first, then cancel the nonzero constant two

00:00:44.311 --> 00:00:51.167
One distance increasing can force the other to decrease because the ladder length stays fixed.

00:00:52.467 --> 00:01:01.333
At horizontal distance three and height four, an outward speed of one gives a downward speed of three quarters

00:01:01.333 --> 00:01:03.667
The negative sign describes direction

00:01:03.667 --> 00:01:08.800
Substituting fixed positions before differentiating would incorrectly erase their time dependence.
